//!
//! GENERATED by `tools/onig-bench --example gen_mbclen` from libonig, which
//! is the specification: this crate is a remake of Oniguruma, so how many
//! bytes a lead spans is whatever Oniguruma says it spans. Do not edit by
//! hand; regenerate.
//!
//! `LEN_<enc>[b0]` is the character length for that first byte. A byte that
//! starts nothing valid reports 1 -- Oniguruma does not raise on undecodable
//! input, it treats the byte as a one-byte character, and so must we.

